.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KZFS-TEST 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kzfs-test
.Nd run the OpenZFS test suite across six distributions from cached golden images
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Cm golden
.Op Ar distro | Cm all
.Op Ar zfs-source
.Nm
.Cm verify
.Op Ar distro | Cm all
.Nm
.Cm run
.Op Fl -quick | -full
.Op Fl -distro Ar list
.Op Ar zfs-source
.Nm
.Cm status
.Nm
.Cm results
.Op Ar run-id
.Nm
.Cm destroy
.Op Fl -all
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
builds a golden image of each of CentOS, Rocky, Fedora, Debian, Ubuntu
and RHEL with ZFS and its test suite, once, and then runs
.Ql zfs-tests.sh
in clones of them, several distributions at a time, recording a matrix of
results.
ZFS can come from the distribution, a release, a git branch or a local
tarball, so a change can be tried across every distribution before it
is sent upstream.
With no command it shows a menu.
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm golden Op Ar distro | Cm all
Build the goldens; kept once built.
.It Cm verify Op Ar distro | Cm all
Boot a clone of each golden and check ZFS and the suite are there.
.It Cm run Oo Fl -quick | Fl -full Oc Op Fl -distro Ar list
Run the suite: a subset of about fifteen minutes, or all of it; on every
distribution, or those named with commas.
.It Cm status
The goldens, the test machines and the last results.
.It Cm results Op Ar run-id
A run's matrix.
.It Cm destroy Op Fl -all
Remove the test machines; with
.Fl -all ,
the goldens too.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -zfs-version Ar v
ZFS from a release tarball.
.It Fl -zfs-git Ar owner/repo@branch , Fl -zfs-git Ar @branch
ZFS from a git branch; the short form is a branch of openzfs/zfs.
.It Fl -zfs-tarball Ar path
ZFS from a local tarball.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /root/kzfs-test/
Golden build logs and one directory per run.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 on a failure, named.
